  "script": {
    "segments": [
      {
        "narration": "An AI nearly doubled the number of drawings in this desert. Southern Peru, where the Nazca lines run for thirteen hundred kilometres.",
        "visual_query": "nazca desert peru aerial",
        "visual_fallback": "desert plateau"
      },
      {
        "narration": "They were made by scraping away the reddish pebbles to show the pale ground underneath. Most of the grooves are ten to fifteen centimetres deep.",
        "visual_query": "peruvian desert stony plateau",
        "visual_fallback": "stony desert"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Two thousand years of wind, almost no rain, and the hummingbird scraped into that plain is still sharp. So what were they actually for?",
        "visual_query": "arid peruvian coastal desert",
        "visual_fallback": "dry desert"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Not a star chart. Hawkins and Aveni tested the alignments and found the case too weak. The reading now is religious: paths walked in procession, and figures asking for water.",
        "visual_query": "nazca geoglyph desert lines",
        "visual_fallback": "desert lines"
      },
      {
        "narration": "The 2024 survey confirmed 303 more, small relief figures sitting beside winding trails that lead toward the temple complex at Cahuachi.",
        "visual_query": "peru desert archaeology site",
        "visual_fallback": "desert dig"
      }
    ],
